  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 306 AM EDT Sat Aug 29 2026\n\n===== Heat Builds Next Week =====\n\nThe prolonged dry streak continues for Sunday and into early next \nweek as sfc high pressure remains anchored over the mid-Atlantic \nregion and upper ridging builds over the central US. The main focus \nfor this time period will be the increasing heat by early next week, \nwhere there is growing confidence in daily high temps solidly in the \n90s. Temps on Sunday are forecast to reach the upper 80s to low 90s, \nbut each subsequent day could be slightly hotter by Wednesday with \npotential for mid to upper 90s. Dewpoints will mainly be in the \nupper 60s to lower 70s over this time, which fortunately will help \nkeep our heat indices from becoming oppressive. While it will be \nmuggy, heat index values are mainly expected to range from the upper \n90s to low 100s. The 100-member LREF indicates that there is less \nthan a 10% chance for max heat index values over 100 for Sunday and \nMonday, but those chances start to increase on Monday and Tuesday, \nand peak on Wednesday with roughly a 25-55% chance for most. In \naddition to the afternoon heat, there will likely be little relief \nduring the nighttime hours, with overnight lows in the 70s each \nnight. \n\nDespite dewpoints not being very high, the combination of hot \ntemperatures, little overnight relief, and the prolonged duration of \nheat will likely lead to major heat risk. Major heat risk means that \nanyone without effective cooling or hydration will be prone to heat \nillness. Probabilities vary by location, but there is roughly a 55% \nchance or higher for major heat risk by Tuesday of next week across \nthe area. That probability increases to at least a 70% chance by \nWednesday. Three or more consecutive days of major heat risk will \ntrigger an extreme heat risk, which essentially means the entire \npopulation could be susceptible to heat illness if precautions are \nnot taken, and there could be increased impact to health services. \nBased off our forecast temps, we have a generalized 25% chance of \nextreme heat risk by Wednesday, though the urban areas are closer to \n50%. \n\nWhile we may not reach criteria heat indices next week, the duration \nof this event and subsequent impacts should be considered in making \nany Heat Advisory decisions. No plans on this yet, but will need to \nconsider in following forecast packages. \n\nWe remain dry through Wednesday, with our next precip chances not \nuntil Thursday. There is lower confidence toward the end of the week \nwith temps and precip, but generally expect the 90 degree temps to \ncontinue through the end of next week.",
